---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Resume" description="My Resume">
    <main id="main" class="font-sans leading-relaxed space-y-12 pt-4 md:pt-8 pb-8">
        <h1 class="sr-only">Vaibhav Kubre — Resume</h1>
        <div class="flex justify-end">
            <a
                href="/Vaibhav-Kubre-Resume.pdf"
                download="Vaibhav-Kubre-Resume.pdf"
                class="font-mono text-sm underline"
            >
                ↓ Download PDF
            </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg">
            Senior backend engineer with 5 years at TARS, an enterprise platform for AI agents and
            live chat. Built the first agent backend of its Asimov product, a PII detection model,
            and the multi-region platform it runs on. TypeScript, Python, PostgreSQL, GCP.
        </p>
        <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="font-mono uppercase text-2xl mb-6"># Work Experience</h2>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-baseline gap-x-4">
                <span class="font-mono text-lg">Senior Software Engineer</span>
                <span class="font-mono text-sm text-carbon-lighter">Dec 2021 - Present</span>
            </div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-carbon-light">TARS, Bangalore</div>
            <div class="font-mono uppercase text-sm text-carbon-lighter pt-4">AI and agents</div>
            <div class="space-y-3">
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">AI agent backend.</span> Built the first agent
                    backend for Asimov, the AI agent product at TARS. It ingests large websites,
                    PDFs, CRMs, and other sources, and gives LLM agents RAG and tool use, which
                    turned scripted chatbots into AI-native agents. Tested ingestion on 2,000
                    customer websites. FastAPI, Celery, Weaviate.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">PII detection model.</span> Trained Veil, a 1.19 MB
                    model that finds personal data in customer chats: names, addresses, phone
                    numbers, emails, ID numbers, and card numbers. It runs in 2.6 ms per message
                    inside the backend or in the browser, with nothing else to deploy. It replaced a
                    spaCy NER service that needed its own VM, with 80% fewer false masks.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">Performance.</span> Cut backend CPU per chat turn by
                    50% and support inbox latency by 49% (1,154 ms to 584 ms). Eliminated backend
                    timeouts in the new regions, from 415 in two days to zero.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">Reliability.</span> Fixed the memory leaks that made
                    the Asimov service run out of memory and restart. It now runs for months with
                    flat memory use.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="font-mono uppercase text-sm text-carbon-lighter pt-4">Platform</div>
            <div class="space-y-3">
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">Data residency.</span> Enterprise customers in
                    Qatar, India, and the EU must keep their data in their own region. Designed and
                    launched a full, separate deployment of the product in each one, on GCP with
                    Convex, PostgreSQL, and Tinybird.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">Migrations.</span> Built the tools that move
                    customers from TARS 2.0 to the rebuilt 3.0 platform, and between regions, with
                    checks, resume, and rollback. Moved a large telecom customer's live account with
                    only 8 minutes of read-only time.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">CI/CD.</span> Rebuilt CI/CD for the monorepo. Checks
                    on every pull request went from 30 minutes to under 6, and one tested build
                    ships to all 4 production regions.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="font-mono uppercase text-sm text-carbon-lighter pt-4">
                Product and leadership
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-3">
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">Live chat.</span> Shipped native live chat with
                    chatbot-to-human handoff on web and WhatsApp, plus routing, CSAT, and analytics.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">Security.</span> Led SOC 2 compliance and
                    penetration test remediation. Run monthly LLM-driven security reviews of the
                    whole codebase, which keeps open findings at zero.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="font-semibold">Hiring and mentoring.</span> Ran 2026 intern hiring:
                    shortlisted 200 from 3,000+ applicants, interviewed them, and trained the 5
                    hires who joined the team. Review pull requests and help teammates debug every
                    day: 186 PRs merged and 217 reviewed in 2026.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-baseline gap-x-4 pt-10">
                <span class="font-mono text-lg">Full Stack Engineer</span>
                <span class="font-mono text-sm text-carbon-lighter">Jan 2019 - Nov 2021</span>
            </div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-carbon-light">Freelance</div>
            <p>
                Built an{" "}
                <a href="/work/wonder-learning/" class="underline">
                    LMS
                </a>{" "}
                that moved 20+ schools online, a{" "}
                <a href="/work/taxglobe/" class="underline">
                    community bookstore
                </a>
                , and a{" "}
                <a href="/work/gatearch/" class="underline">
                    mock-exam portal
                </a>
                . Laravel, Vue, MySQL.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="font-mono uppercase text-2xl mb-6"># Side Projects</h2>
            <p>
                <a href="/work/scrcap/" class="font-semibold underline">
                    scrcap
                </a>
                , 2026. Native macOS screenshot tool with a markup editor and scrolling capture.
                Swift.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a href="/work/depot-gato/" class="font-semibold underline">
                    Depot Gato
                </a>
                , 2024. Solo 2D pixel-art tower defense game, with its own art and design document.
                Godot.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a href="/blog/" class="font-semibold underline">
                    Blog
                </a>
                . Engineering notes and essays.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section class="space-y-2">
            <h2 class="font-mono uppercase text-2xl mb-6"># Skills</h2>
            <p>
                <span class="font-semibold">Languages and backend.</span> TypeScript, Python, SQL,
                Node.js, Convex, FastAPI, React, Next.js
            </p>
            <p>
                <span class="font-semibold">Data and cloud.</span> PostgreSQL, MongoDB, ClickHouse,
                Tinybird, Weaviate, Qdrant, GCP, AWS, Cloudflare, Docker, GitHub Actions
            </p>
        </section>
        <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="font-mono uppercase text-2xl mb-6"># Education</h2>
            <div>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-baseline gap-x-4">
                    <span>
                        <span class="font-semibold">B.Tech in Computer Science</span>, 9.3 CGPA
                    </span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm text-carbon-lighter">2019 - 2022</span>
                </div>
                <div class="text-carbon-light">
                    Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Technological University, Maharashtra
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-baseline gap-x-4">
                    <span>
                        <span class="font-semibold">Diploma in Computer Science</span>, 8.0 CGPA
                    </span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm text-carbon-lighter">2015 - 2019</span>
                </div>
                <div class="text-carbon-light">Maharashtra State Board of Technical Education</div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
